RUN_STATUS {"status":"waiting","last":"S8 fix F-V04 F-V05 F-V06 F-V08 F-V10 F-V13 D-55: 1 D-56: 1","result":"blocked","gate":"not passed (phase 6: F-V02 INC-2 not built, F-V03 theme, F-V13 Spring Security not assessed, F-V06 waits on D-57, F-V01 to be re-measured)","next":"/implement US-020 (then US-021, US-022, /review INC-2, /design, /quality-gate, /verify)","waiting":"D-57 (non-blocking for INC-2), D-56 part (c) Spring Security","log":"C:\\Users\\tanej\\Documents\\LAB\\tanej_sdd-workflow_contacts_v001\\02_output\\logs\\run\\053-fix.json","decisions":[{"id":"D-57","text":"## D-57: AC-012-03 passes at once while the \"Delete forever\" dialog hides the page (frozen test defect, F-V06)\n- Timestamp: 2026-11-12\n- Session: S8 fix F-V06\n- Class: approval\n- Type: non-blocking for the session; the test stays flaky until answered\n- Trigger: F-V06. `acceptance/trash-history.spec.ts:48` clicks the confirming \"Delete forever\" and then `expect(row(page, 'Novak')).toHaveCount(0)`, then asks the API. The app keeps the modal dialog open until the DELETE has ended (`ConfirmDialog.tsx`: the dialog closes after `onConfirm`), and Radix marks the page behind a modal `aria-hidden`; role queries ignore hidden elements, so the row count is 0 at once, before the request is answered. The GET then races the DELETE and sometimes finds the contact (200). The server erase is one transaction (`TrashService.erase`), so after the DELETE returns the contact is gone (404). SR-15 holds; this is a test defect, not an erase defect.\n- Options: (1) Approve a change to the frozen test (proposed): wait for the dialog to close before the row assertion, `await expect(dialog(page)).toHaveCount(0);` between the click and the row check, and update `docs/03_acceptance-manifest.sha256`. (2) Change the app so the dialog closes at once and the row stays until the refetch (worse: no busy state while the request runs; not recommended). (3) Leave the test and list the flakiness in the release notes.\n- Human response: pending\n- Resolution: pending\n- Overrides: none"},{"id":"D-56","text":"## D-56: backend dependency scan reports Critical and High advisories (F-V13)\n- Timestamp: 2026-11-11\n- Session: S7 verify (run 1)\n- Class: approval\n- Type: blocking\n- Trigger: `out/logs/verify-backend-depcheck.log` (dependency-check-maven 12.1.6, NVD without key): `spring-core` and `spring-web` 6.2.19 (12 CVEs, up to 9.8), `spring-security-*` 6.5.11 (up to 9.1), DOMPurify 3.2.4 inside `swagger-ui` 5.28.1 (CVE-2026-116803, 10.0). The matches are by CPE and may be false positives; no reachability analysis has been done. D-13 recorded other advisories and does not name these.\n- Options: (1) (proposed) `/fix F-V13` checks, per advisory, whether the affected code is reachable and whether a fixed version exists on the pinned lines (Spring Boot 3.5.x managed versions); it records the result and brings any version change or any lowering of a Critical or High back to you for approval. (2) Move Spring Boot to a newer 3.5.x or 4.x (you name the version; a change to `tech-stack.md`). (3) Accept the open advisories as a known limitation with a reason (needs your approval for every Critical and High).\n- Human response: 1 (`/fix D-56: 1`, 2026-11-12), with a note: the Spring Framework 6.2.19 Criticals were assessed in D-13 (no server-sent events, no XsltView); re-check them, assess spring-security 6.5.11 and DOMPurify in swagger-ui (is swagger-ui served in production?). Any version change comes back to the developer.\n- Resolution: partly assessed, no version changed (S8 fix F-V13, 2026-11-12). (a) Spring Framework 6.2.19 (GHSA-j9f9-w8pj-32f8 SSE, GHSA-pc63-qcmh-9cmg XsltView): code search in `backend/src` finds no `SseEmitter`, no `text/event-stream`, no XSLT view; still not reachable, as in D-13. The 12 CVEs the scanner lists for `spring-core` and `spring-web` are by CPE and were not individually assessed (see below). (b) DOMPurify 3.2.4 in `swagger-ui` 5.28.1: it is browser JavaScript in the springdoc webjar, used only by the Swagger UI page. `application.yml` sets `springdoc.swagger-ui.enabled: false` and no other file serves the UI, so the page is not served; in production the backend has no published port (`docker-compose.prod.yml`), only the proxy and the web app are reachable. Not reachable; the jar is only on the classpath. I did not request the page on the running backend (the command needed approval), so this rests on the configuration. (c) Spring Security 6.5.11 (CVE-2026-59270 at 9.1, CVE-2026-47841 and CVE-2026-41707 at 7.4, two more below 7): **not assessed**. The advisory texts and fixed versions are not in the repository and the web search was not permitted in this session, so no reachability statement is made; the app uses `oauth2-resource-server` with the Firebase JWT decoder and a custom filter chain. Needs the developer: either allow a search of the advisories, or name a Boot 3.5.x version to move to (a change to `tech-stack.md`). (d) Proposal for the developer, not applied: replace `springdoc-openapi-starter-webmvc-ui` with `springdoc-openapi-starter-webmvc-api` (same version 2.8.13); the app only needs `/v3/api-docs`, and the swagger-ui and DOMPurify jars would leave the build. F-V13 stays open (High) until (c) is answered.\n- Overrides: none"}]}
